      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the test. It verifies that `getSpecifier` produces `[129, 12, 13]` for a `RunCodec(k=13)` where both the A and B codecs are canonical codec #13 (i.e., `BHSDCodec(4, 256)`), and that same codec is the default. I'll rename variables and reorder assertions for clarity.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version replaces cryptic auto-generated names (`bHSDCodec0`, `runCodec0`, `intArray0`) with descriptive ones (`canonicalCodec13`, `runCodec`, `specifier`), moves `assertNotNull` before `assertArrayEquals` so the null check comes first, and adds a Javadoc comment explaining the encoding math that produces `[129, 12, 13]`."
